record legeos.evidence.arrangements-fullscreen-clean-20260831/1 : evidence {
    title "Fullscreen stays clean: no arrangement chrome outside Home, fullscreen windows never arranged"
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:f3233a772c5765a59bf25e0c5a21cb5718511573
    summary """
        Fullscreen windows are excluded from arrangement eligibility (WindowService::arrangement_eligible filters window.fullscreen), and the arrangement controls live on the Home Field's secondary-click menu inside the Home surface — no ShellOverlay surface, no exclusive zone, no reserved strip exists for them — so a fullscreen application occupies its output with no arrangement chrome visible, by construction.
        """
}

record legeos.evidence.d2-archive-verify-20260903/1 : evidence {
    title "D2: archive verification catches mixed sets, missing components, tampered pool files and an unfinished publish"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    command "cargo test -p lege repo && cargo run -q -p lege -- dev --repo <tmp>/archive repo init && ... repo publish --build-set target/debian/build-set.json && ... repo verify"
    summary """
        `lege dev repo verify` detects the failures it exists for. 31 lege tests pass under the `repo` filter (all pre-existing archive tests plus verify-detects-mixed-set and verify-detects-missing-component, the latter verifying from Matrix::embedded() with no source checkout). End to end in a tempdir archive with real gpg and apt-ftparchive: a real 13-package set published, sets/<id>/debs created with all 13 hard links, verify reported current ok with 13 pins; appending 8 bytes to a pool .deb produced "is 8578088 bytes, but the manifest recorded 8578080" plus "the pool no longer matches Packages" and exit 1; deleting a pool file produced "is gone from the pool"; a hand-written staged marker produced "staged but never became current". Nothing outside the tempdir was touched.
        """
}

record legeos.evidence.d2-source-build-not-executed-20260903/1 : evidence {
    title "D2: ci/source-build.sh exists but was not executed — no chroot backend on this host"
    state verified
    result inconclusive
    method command
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    command "ci/source-build.sh"
    summary """
        The clean-root source build did NOT run on this host: neither mmdebstrap nor podman is installed, so ci/source-build.sh printed "NOT EXECUTED (neither mmdebstrap nor podman is installed on this host)" and exited 0 without building anything. The lane is written and syntax-checked (bash -n) and is wired into ci/run.sh, but no Ubuntu 26.04 source build has been observed and none is claimed. Running it needs `sudo apt-get install mmdebstrap` (or podman) and is a user-run step.
        """
}

record legeos.evidence.d2-version-authority-20260903/1 : evidence {
    title "D2: one version authority — changelog derived from the build-set id, guarded in debian/rules"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    command "cargo test -p lege-build && just deb-plan && cargo run -q -p xtask -- archive changelog --write <tmp>/debian/changelog --epoch 1788400000 && LEGEOS_BUILD_SET_ID=0.1.0~dev1788400000+g8b284c9.dirty make -f debian/rules override_dh_auto_configure"
    summary """
        The debian/changelog head entry is generated from the BuildSetId and the source build refuses to disagree with it: 22 lege-build tests pass including the derivation test; `just deb-plan` prints build set 0.1.0~dev1788441091+g8b284c9.dirty and the changelog head line carrying that same id; `cargo xtask archive changelog --write` into a disposable copy produced that stanza, and debian/rules' configure guard printed "changelog and build set agree" for the matching id and exited 1 with "debian/changelog says … but the build set is …" for a mismatched one.
        """
}

