record legeos.evidence.hardware-probe-tests-20260903/1 : evidence {
    title "The probe module, the four-outcome report and the boot-health delegation are green: 9 + 36 + 23 + 4 tests pass"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    command "cargo test -p lege-hwdetect; cargo test -p lege doctor::; cargo test -p lege-boot-health; cargo test -p lege-hostd --test hardware_matrix"
    summary """
        lege-hwdetect 9/9 (7 pre-existing plus the two new probe properties: a timed-out probe is NotExecuted, never Fail; a missing binary is Skipped, never Fail or Pass). lege doctor:: 36/36, including the four pre-existing hardware tests and the new one asserting a single fixture report contains all four outcomes and that no tests/hardware case is ever reported as executed. lege-boot-health 23/23 unchanged after its four probe functions were made thin wrappers over lege-hwdetect::probes — a timeout still maps to Status::Fail there, so the promotion and forced-reboot logic is untouched. lege-hostd hardware_matrix 4/4 after three manual cases were added from X1's C6 matrix. rustfmt clean on every file touched; clippy clean on lege-hwdetect and lege-boot-health (the three lege warnings are in cli/lege/src/dev, D5's lane).
        """
}

record legeos.evidence.hardware-qualification-report-20260903/1 : evidence {
    title "lege doctor --hardware now executes ten bounded read-only probes and emits one four-outcome report; every manual case is not-executed"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    command "cargo run -q -p lege -- doctor --hardware --json"
    summary """
        On the Intel Iris Xe + RTX 4060 Laptop dev host: 39 findings — 20 pass, 1 fail, 7 skipped, 11 not executed (report kept at .agent/scratch/de01/D4-doctor-hardware.json via `akr scratch keep`). Ten probes ran read-only and timeout-bounded: kernel-release (6.17.0-41-generic), drm-connected-output (card2-eDP-2), drm-modesetting, nvidia-module (610.43.02 matches nvidia-driver-610-open), nvidia-smi (RTX 4060 Laptop GPU), vulkan-devices (3 devices), prime-offload (available, not exercised), vaapi (59 profiles, Intel iHD 25.4.5) all passed; cuda-device-query was skipped (deviceQuery is not installed). nvidia-module-signer FAILED: the module is signed by a locally enrolled MOK with no linux-modules-nvidia-* package installed — this host is DKMS-built, which LegeOS forbids. All eleven tests/hardware cases were emitted as not-executed with their steps. NOTHING MANUAL RAN: no suspend, reboot, GPU-mode change, cable operation or driver change was performed or attempted, and no hardware case may be read as passed.
        """
}

